{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365909-what-are-chimera-in-3rd-edition","id":1365909,"title":"What are Chimera in 3rd Edition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-02-06T18:52:30-08:00","id":1365909,"title":"What are Chimera in 3rd Edition?","content":"I've always felt conflicted about Chimera in 2nd Edition. The idea of some Lunars devolving into protean horrors due to Wyld exposure was tragically interesting, but it always felt weird that Lunars were supposed to be dealing with the Wyld quite a bit &amp; had less immunity to it then their patron goddess.<br /> <br /> I've had many alternative ideas about how Chimera might come to pass for home-brew, but they all had their issues.<br /> <br /> How has 3rd Edition handled the concept &amp; origin of Chimera? I heard it is quite different. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T19:01:42-08:00","id":1365912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365909-what-are-chimera-in-3rd-edition#post1365909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How has 3rd Edition handled the concept &amp; origin of Chimera? I heard it is quite different.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the whole idea of the Lunar Exaltations being warped by the Wyld, and the tattoos being necessary to correct that has been completely dropped. The moonsilver tattoos and the current set of Lunar castes that they create are presented as an active step that the Lunars took to adapt to the post-Usurpation landscape. They decided that their old castes didn't work anymore, so they came up with a new set, and the tattoos are the way they set them (and there's some hints that changing the castes happened before, possibly just after the war against the Primordials). Casteless Lunars now don't risk mutation or derangement when shapeshifting. They get access to some caste powers from all three of the current Castes, though on a shifting schedule, and they don't get Caste Attributes (but do get slightly cheaper attributes and charms that are non-favored). <br /> <br /> Chimeras, rather than being linked to Castelessness, are instead <i>any</i> Lunar who's spirit shape is a combination of two different animals rather than a single beast (which is represented by taking the charm Chimera-Soul Expression). So Ma-Ha-Suchi, for example, is a chimera, because his spirit shape is a hybrid of goat and wolf.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T19:04:55-08:00","id":1365914,"title":"","content":"Now, a Chimera is just any Lunar with the Essence 1 Universal Charm <i>Chimera-Soul Expression</i>, which lets them mix a second animal into their spirit-shape, applying some merits to represent the added traits; those traits are also present in <i>Hybrid Body Transformation</i>. Instead of being degenerate mutant monsters, it's just a representation of how some Lunars' spirit shapes are or become more than just natural beasts. It's very neat, because you can just be a Chimera if you want, and that just means your Lunar nature pushes at the limits of the animal kingdom.<br /> EDIT: The things that Kelly said also!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T19:50:06-08:00","id":1365928,"title":"","content":"Honestly, chimera even as a term for Lunars with hybrid spirit shapes seems to be more of an inference by readers based on past experiences than an element of the setting. I don't believe that the word is ever used in Fangs at the Gate to describe a Lunar.<br /> <br /> Considering the casual attitude the current Edition has to the Charm in question and the baggage carried from prior ones, I think it may be better to not use the term as a specific noun for Lunars, to avoid some confusion.<br /> <br /> A hybrid spirit shape also gives a Lunar a second animal to decide on whether or not they can buy Totem Charms with an alternative Attribute.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T20:20:08-08:00","id":1365930,"title":"","content":"I have notes on a Shogunate era setting and including \u201cWyld Exalted\u201d monsters based on 2E Chimera derived from Lunars, but no more reflecting Lunars in general being \u201cWyld tainted\u201d than Abyssals mean Solars in general are \u201cUnderworld tainted\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T20:45:37-08:00","id":1365932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365909-what-are-chimera-in-3rd-edition?p=1365928#post1365928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, chimera even as a term for Lunars with hybrid spirit shapes seems to be more of an inference by readers based on past experiences than an element of the setting. I don't believe that the word is ever used in Fangs at the Gate to describe a Lunar.<br /> <br /> Considering the casual attitude the current Edition has to the Charm in question and the baggage carried from prior ones, I think it may be better to not use the term as a specific noun for Lunars, to avoid some confusion.<br /> <br /> A hybrid spirit shape also gives a Lunar a second animal to decide on whether or not they can buy Totem Charms with an alternative Attribute.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it's basically what they were in 1e. I think it's just as much pointing out that return in definition than anything else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T22:34:57-08:00","id":1365947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365909-what-are-chimera-in-3rd-edition?p=1365932#post1365932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, it's basically what they were in 1e. I think it's just as much pointing out that return in definition than anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>No! No they were not! I'm going to get to that book's Charms chapter one day and expect it will tie the spirit shape Charms back to the concept in some manner, but otherwise the First Edition concept for chimaera was almost identical to that of Second Edition, it just wasn't heavily systemized and could only happen to you in the Wyld.<br /> <br /> The basic idea was still that Casteless Lunars exposed out there were very vulnerable to becoming mindless monsters riddled with mutations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-06T23:01:18-08:00","id":1365949,"title":"","content":"Ah, my apologies, I myself had forgotten that the portion of Exalted: the Lunars I have read so far did actually clarify on the point.<br /> <br /> Lunars that had cultivated hybrid totems <i>were</i> called chimera... in the sense of &quot;we're pejoratively comparing you to or outright accusing you of being this otherwise separate stigmatized category&quot;.<br /> <br /> A chimera was a Lunar who had lost their mind and in a state of almost constantly shapeshifting. A Lunar with a hybrid totem was supposed to be somebody who looked vaguely similar enough to that for other Lunars to be put on edge by the resemblance, or even think that the hybrid totems was actively seeking to become a chimera.<br /> <br /> So there was chimera the being and chimera the slur.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 02-07-2020, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T06:43:14-08:00","id":1366002,"title":"","content":"Ah. So there are no Lunars who have become protean horrors in 3rd Edition at all. I see.<br /> <br /> If my memory serves, I remember Holden &amp; Hatewheel stating a way back they were going to create a new reason for &quot;Chimeras&quot; (monster Lunars), but I guess it didn't make the release.<br /> <br /> A pity, as I was curious what they where going to create.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T07:01:07-08:00","id":1366005,"title":"","content":"Well, never say never.<br /> <br /> But to become a protean horror in 3e a lunar has to <i>work at it.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T08:07:15-08:00","id":1366024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365909-what-are-chimera-in-3rd-edition?p=1366002#post1366002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah. So there are no Lunars who have become protean horrors in 3rd Edition at all. </div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't say that. There's no mechanical <i>necessity </i>for some of them to go that way, true, but their charms absolutely can go down that path. It's just that now, &quot;protean horror&quot; is more of a one-off character concept that the ST can choose to put in, or a player decide to lean into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T08:32:50-08:00","id":1366032,"title":"","content":"I suppose if a Casteless Lunar went and spent years in the Deep Wyld, they'd still become a protean horror (possibly, they equally might also end up looking like a My Little Pony character) if they didn't know/use the integrity protection charms.<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T09:08:52-08:00","id":1366041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365909-what-are-chimera-in-3rd-edition?p=1366032#post1366032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suppose if a Casteless Lunar went and spent years in the Deep Wyld, they'd still become a protean horror (possibly, they equally might also end up looking like a My Little Pony character) if they didn't know/use the integrity protection charms.<br /> <br /> prototype00</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying My Little Pony characters are <i>not</i> protean horrors?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;At the risk of sounding like a murder hobo&quot;<br /> <br /> Attributed to Nyrufa.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24134-inertial-frame","name":"Inertial Frame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T09:48:51-08:00","id":1366054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365909-what-are-chimera-in-3rd-edition?p=1366002#post1366002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my memory serves, I remember Holden &amp; Hatewheel stating a way back they were going to create a new reason for &amp;quot;Chimeras&amp;quot; (monster Lunars), but I guess it didn't make the release.<br /> <br /> A pity, as I was curious what they where going to create.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there was a thing Holden described once on RPG.Net that I focused on for a long time about the mental state of a Lunar who stayed Casteless for too long. That was probably somewhere around their ideas for what the equivalent was going to be like, and I found the description compelling.<br /> <br /> Looking at Fangs at the Gate, I suspect it was the kind of thing that was drummed out on the whole when they placed the strongest emphasis on Lunar relationships, and their cultural and political context. Probably also a point at which a decision needed to be made about incompatible paths for the Casteless to take. It's similar to how the focus on Rage was more understated, and basically no follow up to that core book stuff about them being so hung up on the Old Realm in a mystical sense.<br /> <br /> Those were all products I attached to, but I really do think the final product is stronger without them. I think the narrative for Lunar characters and powers is a lot stronger when centered on the idea that they're filled with dichotomies but essentially in control. Lunars are still capable of doing so kinds of terrifying shit, and you can generally be sure that they meant to.<br /> <br /> That and the Dominions are just sublime.<br /> <br /> I think Monstrous Urge, their version of the Great Curse, might cover a few of the bases. Tattoos won't protect you from that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kelly Pedersen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365909-what-are-chimera-in-3rd-edition?p=1366024#post1366024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't say that. There's no mechanical <i>necessity </i>for some of them to go that way, true, but their charms absolutely can go down that path. It's just that now, &amp;quot;protean horror&amp;quot; is more of a one-off character concept that the ST can choose to put in, or a player decide to lean into.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really only just in a couple of the swarm Charms, isn't it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T09:56:02-08:00","id":1366056,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't say they're so much protean horrors, as Chimeric horrors (appropriately), with the characteristics of dozens of beasts large and small, mammalian and alien, grafted together to make a horror out of nightmare.<br /> It's not... not protean, but it's not like a formless horror that can become anything.<br /> <br /> For example, most of their mutation charms only deal with mutations based on your known forms. So you might walk into battle with the claws of a wolverine, the skin of a rhino, tentacles and spider-legs, antannae and hawk eyes and a beak full of fanged teeth that inject neuro-toxin, not to mention shoot strands of web or belch out a swarm of angry wasps... but you can't have iron skin, a bone-gun that shoots burrowing bugs, tentacles covered in glass shards, a shadow-maw of flint teeth, and four necrotic zombie-legs.<br /> <br /> You're not a Tzimisce, or a Tyranid, or a Shoggoth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T11:21:46-08:00","id":1366074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365909-what-are-chimera-in-3rd-edition?p=1366056#post1366056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not... not protean, but it's not like a formless horror that can become anything.<br /> <br /> For example, most of their mutation charms only deal with mutations based on your known forms. So you might walk into battle with the claws of a wolverine, the skin of a rhino, tentacles and spider-legs, antannae and hawk eyes and a beak full of fanged teeth that inject neuro-toxin, not to mention shoot strands of web or belch out a swarm of angry wasps... but you can't have iron skin, a bone-gun that shoots burrowing bugs, tentacles covered in glass shards, a shadow-maw of flint teeth, and four necrotic zombie-legs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, note that you can use supernatural merits gained from forms of mutated animals or humans (though you have to commit extra motes, of course). Honestly, most of the things you just described are things I could see mutated creatures from the Wyld as having. So a Lunar who spent a long, long time out in the Marches, taking mutant forms, could very well have a large library of supernatural mutations to add to their forms. I do agree that a Lunar can't take any forms that they haven't captured, but that's still a very, very long list, once you take the weirdness of Creation into account.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T11:58:16-08:00","id":1366083,"title":"","content":"Hmmmmmmmmmmmm..........<br /> <br /> That's a very useful point, thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T13:57:32-08:00","id":1366106,"title":"","content":"Going by the Supernatural Merits published thus far, I think that in most cases the point at which mutations are incorporating inorganic materials or mystical features is the point where you're becoming magical enough to no longer qualify for the Sacred Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T15:47:15-08:00","id":1366140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365909-what-are-chimera-in-3rd-edition?p=1365947#post1365947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No! No they were not! I'm going to get to that book's Charms chapter one day and expect it will tie the spirit shape Charms back to the concept in some manner, but otherwise the First Edition concept for chimaera was almost identical to that of Second Edition, it just wasn't heavily systemized and could only happen to you in the Wyld.<br /> <br /> The basic idea was still that Casteless Lunars exposed out there were very vulnerable to becoming mindless monsters riddled with mutations.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing of note in 1e to 2e is that in 1e, chimerism was well...chimerism. Becoming a blend of multiple animals. While in 2e, it's a stage to eventaully becoming a Shuggoth or Alex Mercer. I think the statement <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2402_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2402\" data-vbnamecard=\"2402\">The Wizard of Oz</a>'s comment on protean v. chimeric is a bit there. While there's not the same stigma, I think the <i>aesthetic</i> of 3e chimeras feels more like the 1e one, which to me implied Lunars going down the route of like, monsterous beats rather than flesh blob horrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-07T22:11:37-08:00","id":1366241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1365909-what-are-chimera-in-3rd-edition?p=1366140#post1366140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing of note in 1e to 2e is that in 1e, chimerism was well...chimerism. Becoming a blend of multiple animals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well now that blend was described as shifting so continuously that they were nicknamed &quot;the Formless ones&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While in 2e, it's a stage to eventaully becoming a Shuggoth or Alex Mercer.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, looking back on the Chimera Knacks, they didn't exactly seem useful enough to be in all the time. Quicksilver Form let you turn into a pile of goo... which is described primarily in terms of being able to flow through cracks and becoming less vulnerable to blades but more to bludgeoning. Assimilation of the Prey is... actually pretty weird, it doesn't provide an actual mechanism to engulfing a target so you can just basically walk over to somebody and kill them in a few ticks without a defence or any resistance beyond hurting the Lunar enough for them to leave. Grotesque Pseudopodia at least provides tentacles for ranged Martial Arts attacks.<br /> <br /> But they're all still temporary; the default form and core narrative of the Chimera still remained being a Lunar covered in mutations and with an innate power to acquire more at will.<br /> <br /> Looking back on those Knacks... sure they're very flashy, but they don't do all that much. Most of them end up being weird, kind of inferior Charms. I suppose I can get the logic of &quot;hey, if they get freaky undulating flesh, maybe some shapeshifting to expand on that&quot;, but it's still a pretty narrow repertoire. I think in a lot of cases it was more useful to stay in a shape that you could stack Strength and speed enhancing mutations on.<br /> <br /> The shoggoth thing isn't in the (ultimately not very long) text nearly as much as it predominated in internet conversations. Far from being something that came across as an ultimate end point for them. And it wasn't as if any other book developed them further, because what more was there to say?<br /> <br /> (Oy, I had to go digging in The Pile to find my copy of Manual: Lunars)<br /> <br /> All of this stuff being my basis for why calling Lunars with hybrid spirit shapes in Third Edition is liable to be misleading, and would not be a call back to a thing they were in First Edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blaque</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">While there's not the same stigma, I think the <i>aesthetic</i> of 3e chimeras feels more like the 1e one, which to me implied Lunars going down the route of like, monsterous beats rather than flesh blob horrors.</div> </div> </div> </div>All the things I've said above aside, sure the aesthetic is similar. After all, the original hybrid Lunars were also perceived in-character to have a similar aesthetic. It was a perception the text noted to be an error of the characters, and that changing your totem was unrelated to the actual condition of being a chimera.<br /> <br /> The <i>narrative</i> of being an actual chimera was something else, something the two Editions had more in common with one another, and that doesn't exist in Third Edition at all.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... but I'm now thinking in getting a bit too hung up on this. That in the total absence of a narrative of &quot;Lunars who lost their mind and get in a state of constantly shifting form&quot;, the orphaned term of chimera is ready to be wholly adopted to refer to Lunars with a pair of totems. I talked about baggage, but the person from this thread adapted quickly.<br /> <br /> Jeez, I if people remember First Edition chimeras as something mistaken but then all say &quot;Third Edition is just like his it was back then&quot;, does the original version matter all that much?<br /> <br /> Why are you so hung up on this, Levi? Are you, what, angry that First Edition Lunars turned out to be different on several points than the Internet whispering game told you it would be? Go to sleep already.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}